(go/type Value "A Value represents a value in the SSA representation of the program.\nThe ID and Type fields must not be modified. The remainder may be modified\nif they preserve the value of the Value (e.g. changing a (mul 2 x) to an (add x x)).\n" (struct


    ^{:line 24 :tag ID :doc "A unique identifier for the value. For performance we allocate these IDs\ndensely starting at 1.  There is no guarantee that there won't be occasional holes, though.\n"} ID


    ^{:line 27 :tag Op :doc "The operation that computes this value. See op.go.\n"} Op



    ^{:line 31 :tag (* types/Type) :doc "The type of this value. Normally this will be a Go type, but there\nare a few other pseudo-types, see ../types/type.go.\n"} Type








    ^{:line 40 :tag int64 :doc "Auxiliary info for this value. The type of this information depends on the opcode and type.\nAuxInt is used for integer values, Aux is used for other values.\nFloats are stored in AuxInt using math.Float64bits(f).\nUnused portions of AuxInt are filled by sign-extending the used portion,\neven if the represented value is unsigned.\nUsers of AuxInt which interpret AuxInt as unsigned (e.g. shifts) must be careful.\nUse Value.AuxUnsigned to get the zero-extended value of AuxInt.\n"} AuxInt
    ^{:line 41 :tag Aux} Aux


    ^{:line 44 :tag (slice (* Value)) :doc "Arguments of this value\n"} Args


    ^{:line 47 :tag (* Block) :doc "Containing basic block\n"} Block


    ^{:line 50 :tag src/XPos :doc "Source position\n"} Pos


    ^{:line 53 :tag int32 :doc "Use count. Each appearance in Value.Args and Block.Controls counts once.\n"} Uses



    ^{:line 57 :tag bool :doc "wasm: Value stays on the WebAssembly stack. This value will not get a \"register\" (WebAssembly variable)\nnor a slot on Go stack, and the generation of this value is delayed to its use time.\n"} OnWasmStack


    ^{:line 60 :tag bool :doc "Is this value in the per-function constant cache? If so, remove from cache before changing it or recycling it.\n"} InCache


    ^{:line 63 :tag (array 3 (* Value)) :doc "Storage for the first three args\n"} argstorage))


